# Release ISO runs in the background

The image build and the GitHub attachment already work. When a release
needs an ISO, start `scripts/iso-release.sh` in the background and
continue.

Do not poll the build, wait for it to finish, or report back about the
image, the upload, or the checksum. The script checks the upload itself.

Do not start an ISO build during ordinary development just to confirm
the pipeline.
